 {"id":"fabro-5e09","title":"Develop planner: pick only seeds assigned to fabro (sd ready --assignee fabro) — deterministic line/user ownership split","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:16:32.837Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:07:20.678Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"GRILL SETTLED 2026-09-07 (user decisions in session):\n\nDECIDED: (D1) The assignee filter for the develop workflow is APPROVED — 'sd ready --assignee fabro' becomes the planner's candidate source. (D2) The REVISOR ASSIGNS NOBODY: filing seeds is its job, ownership is NOT — revisor-filed seeds land UNASSIGNED in the backlog. (D3) Who executes a seed is decided JOINTLY by user + agent (cycle report / grill / chat is the forum; the agent's @fabro assignment is a proposal the user can veto by reassigning anytime). (D4) Fail-closed default (Opt-in): nothing belongs to the line until @fabro is explicitly set. (D5) Emergency channel stays as the standing user directive: when the line/engine is DOWN the agent repairs directly with the user's knowledge (no seed picker involved); the seed is filed retroactively for documentation. No emergency self-service class exists for the revisor or the line.\n\nMECHANISM (line implements, from D1): (1) develop planner prompt candidate source: 'sd ready --assignee fabro --limit 200' (CLI pre-filters — the LLM never sees unassigned/user-owned seeds); (2) goal fast-path honors a named seed id ONLY when assignee is fabro; (3) claim: 'sd update <id> --status in_progress --assignee fabro'; (4) Tracker-empty on the filtered view = legitimate end of work (park) — while the backlog is unassigned the line does NOTHING rather than something; (5) docs/agents/issue-tracker.md documents: assignee is the ownership switch; filers (agent, revisor) file UNASSIGNED; assignment is a joint user+agent decision recorded in the cycle report; (6) revisor seed-intake prompt: remove any language implying the revisor decides execution — it only files.\n\nOWNERSHIP (user decides, NOT the implementer): the existing backlog assignment list is a user+agent joint decision (category proposal from the agent, approval by the user); NO bulk-assign by the develop run. Sentinels (fabro-919b/fabro-80cc) stay until mechanism landed AND backlog curated.\n\nAcceptance: planner prompt ships the filtered command; an unassigned or user-assigned open seed never appears in develop candidates; empty filtered view parks; revisor files unassigned; docs updated; ownership list untouched by the implementer.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-d5fd","title":"Develop planner: probe unfiltered sd list before parking on an empty assignee-filtered view","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:16:29.219Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:26:05.721Z","description":"This run's implementer smoke test showed 'sd ready --assignee nonexistentuser' exits 0 with \"No ready issues.\" — byte-identical to a legitimately empty pool — so under the new park semantics a typo'd or renamed assignee silently parks the line forever. Change: in the FAIL-CLOSED paragraph at .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md:46, before routing Tracker empty, run one unfiltered 'sd list --limit 5' probe; if open seeds exist but the filtered view is empty, journal \"park: N open seeds, none assigned to fabro\" so the terminal Slack notification shows a cause. Effect: converts a silent permanent outage into a visible, diagnosable park; zero added cost in normal runs. Related: fabro-5e09 (the assignee filter this builds on).\nBasis: run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9, workflow version 2232aaf05c7a93b3557b65ef13543486edcf917d0a735f9cb430280339b647a2, commit 6677e200fb8d35e90c2a554bdebe0edc69340394","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-bbbb","title":"Develop planner: drop reasoning_effort from high to low for first-pass claims","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:16:29.325Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:41:57.947Z","description":"In run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9 the planner was the most expensive stage (83.6 s wall = 40% of run, $0.080 = 45% of cost, 4,469 of 5,899 reasoning tokens), mostly tie-breaking two High seeds. The assignee filter this run shipped (fabro-5e09, PR #38) makes 'sd ready --assignee fabro' deterministic, so the tie-break reasoning is wasted. Change: set reasoning_effort=\"low\" on the planner node at .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro:49 (keep high semantics for changes_requested re-plans if conditional effort isn't available; re-measure one run). Effect: ~$0.03-0.05 and 20-40 s off every claim pass.\nBasis: run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9, workflow version 2232aaf05c7a93b3557b65ef13543486edcf917d0a735f9cb430280339b647a2, commit 6677e200fb8d35e90c2a554bdebe0edc69340394","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-07T13:41:57.947Z"}
-{"id":"fabro-513e","title":"Add a just validate-workflows recipe for graph-only validation without a Rust cold build","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:40:03.195Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:43.642Z","description":"In run 01M1XVXF3MJHD0DXVCA7YXDH9G the implementer verified a pure workflow-graph edit by writing a temp integration test lib/components/fabro-validate/tests/tmp_validate_develop.rs and running it: 427,565 ms (~7.1 min cold build), one failure on unresolved_file_ref (@prompts refs), warm re-run 2.9s, then manual deletion — 427s of the 445s implementer tool time (~25% of run wall). Add a just validate-workflows recipe (justfile + small nu wrapper around fabro-validate) that resolves workflow-relative @-refs or scopes out unresolved_file_ref so graph edits verify in seconds. Expected effect: ~7 min and the temp-file dance eliminated on every platform-targeting seed (most of the tracker's High queue); implementer wall drops ~30% on that seed class. Basis: run 01M1XVXF3MJHD0DXVCA7YXDH9G, workflow version 8afe037fc8c61680097f808a27f66ee20da8b546373f6e6e69ad4a09aee94a98, commit 9655d15457db349b4920de1f37eb76338e43eab9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
